### How do you register a shutdown hook?

```java
Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
    System.out.println("Shutdown hook: flushing buffers...");
    auditBuffer.flush();
    connectionPool.close();
}));
```

The thread must be created but not started; the JVM starts it during shutdown.

### When does it run and when does it not?

| Trigger | Hook Runs? |
|---------|------------|
| Last non-daemon thread finishes | Yes |
| System.exit(code) | Yes |
| SIGTERM (Kubernetes pod stop) | Yes |
| Ctrl-C (SIGINT) | Yes |
| kill -9 (SIGKILL) | No |
| Power loss | No |
| Native JVM crash (segfault) | No |

### What is the graceful shutdown pattern?

```java
package com.bank.shutdown;

import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

public class GracefulShutdown {

    private volatile boolean running = true;
    private final ExecutorService executor;

    public GracefulShutdown(ExecutorService executor) {
        this.executor = executor;
        Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(this::shutdown));
    }

    private void shutdown() {
        running = false;
        executor.shutdown();  // stop accepting new tasks
        try {
            if (!executor.awaitTermination(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
                executor.shutdownNow();  // interrupt stragglers
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            executor.shutdownNow();
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
        System.out.println("Shutdown complete.");
    }
}
```

### What are common mistakes?

```java
// WRONG: calling System.exit inside a hook (deadlocks)
Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
    cleanup();
    System.exit(0);  // DEADLOCK: shutdown is already in progress
}));

// WRONG: relying on hook for critical data
Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
    saveUncommittedPayments();  // may not run on kill -9!
}));
```

